                            13.Non-Functional Requirements

NFR-01: Performance
The system shall respond to user requests within 3 seconds under normal operating conditions.
Customer registration, vehicle registration, job card creation, quotation generation, and payment recording shall be completed without noticeable delay.
Vehicle status updates shall be available to customers within 5 seconds of a mechanic updating the status.

NFR-02: Availability
The system shall be available 99% of operating hours excluding planned maintenance.
Customers shall be able to access vehicle progress information at any time when internet connectivity is available.
Notification services shall be operational whenever the system is available.

NFR-03: Security
All users shall authenticate before accessing protected system features.
Customer, vehicle, quotation, and payment information shall only be accessible to authorized users.
Passwords shall be encrypted before storage.
Communication between Flutter, ASP.NET, and Supabase shall use secure HTTPS connections.

NFR-04: Usability
The system shall provide a simple and intuitive interface requiring minimal training.
Customers shall be able to locate vehicle status information within three navigation steps.
System screens shall maintain a consistent design throughout the application.

NFR-05: Reliability
The system shall accurately store and retrieve all job cards, quotations, and payment records.
No customer, vehicle, or repair information shall be lost during normal system operation.
Data shall remain consistent across all user roles.

NFR-06: Maintainability
The application shall be developed using a modular architecture to simplify future enhancements.
Code shall be documented to support future maintenance and upgrades.
Errors and exceptions shall be logged for troubleshooting purposes.

NFR-07: Scalability
The system shall support growth in the number of customers, vehicles, job cards, and quotations without requiring significant redesign.
The database shall allow future expansion to support additional workshop branches.

NFR-08: Compatibility
The customer application shall run on Android devices.
The web version shall support Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Mozilla Firefox.
The system shall function correctly across different screen sizes.

NFR-09: Notification Delivery
Email and in-app notifications shall be delivered within one minute of a vehicle status changing to "Ready for Collection".
Notification failures shall be recorded in system logs for administrative review.

NFR-10: Data Accuracy and Transparency
Quotations shall display labour and parts costs clearly and accurately.
Any discount resulting from customer-supplied parts shall be calculated automatically.
Cost calculations shall remain consistent across all quotations.



